past.employee_description:
-  Regional KAM team leadership (MG, DF, GO, TO, MS and MT area).
-  Service delivery management in Sustainable Fleet Management by leading a group of 11 consultants (Ecofrotas);
- Manage, mentor, coach and support account consultants development;
- Technical and strategic support to the largest company negotiations nationwide;
- Definition, implementation and management of after-sales processes;
- Implementation project management in the largest companies nationwide (Fuel Control and Maintenance Control systems);
- Sustain rapport with key accounts by making periodic visits; explore specific needs; anticipating new opportunities;
- Work closely with Product Manager to identify customer application needs regarding new products, sales tools, and required services;
- Development of new opportunities (cross and up selling) within the customer portfolio.

- Regional sales team leadership;
- Manage, mentor, coach and support sales executives development;
- Lead monthly business review process to drive continuous improvement in sales and overall business performance;
- Forecast sales revenues on a monthly and annual basis; 
- Lead and contribute to strategic commercial negotiation (core listing, annual pricing, payment terms, cost savings, supply agreements);
- Develop strong relationships with existing partners as well as engaging at all levels of the company (Key system integrators and Enterprise accounts), with a “win-win” approach; 
- Work with marketing, product management, pre-sales, after-sales and professional services teams to maximize opportunities and foster cohesive sales strategies;
- Drive prospects and customer visits for technical product presentations, demonstrations, demos, reference boards and application manuals;
- Understand specific market and customer environment and specific customer activities, strategies, brands, markets, consumers via multisource (public information, annual reports, press, meetings, etc.);
- Development of new opportunities (cross and up selling) within the customer portfolio;
- General management responsibilities.

The Partnerships and Indirect Sales area maintains and expands relationships with assigned channel partners, based on geography, segment or market. Besides this, the area represents the full range of Fleet & Mobility, Spend Management and HR Benefits products and services for designated partners, creating an aggressive growth strategy that accelerates the business in each partner organization.
The Partnerships and Indirect Sales Manager is responsible for achieving the sales, profitability and partner recruitment goals.

- Traditional distribution (Local, Regional and National);
- Manage, mentor, coach and support Sales and Channel Managers;
- Partnerships around the Brazilian and LATAM market;
- Direct Customers;
- Customer Service;
- Manage existing partners relationship;
- Generate enthusiasm and passion for Fleet & Mobility, Spend Management and HR Benefits products and services among sales and partners;
- Maintain annual and quarterly business plans;
- Develop and supervise marketing and incentive programs to boost sales;
- Coordinate sales and technical training for Partners;
- Facilitate communications and business flow between the Partners and Channel Managers.

- Lead the Business Development | Strategic Segments Sales area to ensure commercial positioning and rapid growth in Brazil;
- Manage complex contract negotiations;
- Create value propositions around company products and services;
- Provide a consultative selling with the customer and partners, aiming to present the spend management solution most appropriate to their needs;
- Working in strategic partnership with regional leaders, product, finance, ops teams and country heads as well as external consultants when needed;
- Support product, finance and ops teams by building and managing relationships and agreements with appropriate clients and partners;
- Driving deep into BR segments to identify and manage strategic business opportunities;
- Sales engagement, attending meetings with clients, key stakeholders and other market participants to influence, identify concerns, opportunities, future market and sales developments;
- Represent Clara in meetings and fairs with executives from other companies.

- Responsible for the KAM team in Brazil by implementing and executing the enablement, engagement and retention processes;
- Understand our product and services and be completely up to speed with all new propositions launched;
- Deeply understand our partners, channels, clients and their operations, what success looks like for them and what we need to do to be able to support their growth;
- Provide leadership and very clear direction to the KAM team;
- Build growth and retention plans for our whole client portfolio, in collaboration with the board and following our commercial guidelines;
- Monitor the execution of the plans through daily / weekly support to the KAMs;
- Scale the team to ensure we have the right set of skills as well as capacity to support our ambitious growth;
- Step in’ to provide support to the KAMs whenever required;
- Bring best practices in terms of client engagement and account development;
- Negotiate contractual terms for renewal, up-sells, cross-sells as required and in line with company guidelines.
- Ensure financial integrity of all client billing processes, in line with contractual agreement;
- Liaise with other areas of the business as appropriate including marketing, legal, onboarding, compliance, CH and finance;
- Work very closely with the other members of the Sales, Partnerships, Credit, Legal, Product, Marketing, Data, CH and Ops team to ensure that any process provide positive impact to the clients, channels and partners.

- Raise new business opportunities with Devex's world team;
- Fine tune the commercial policy for LATAM and North America countries, in close coordination with the Sales Director - LATAM, including price list, discounts, payment terms, pipeline management and product access in order to boost the sales volume;
- Create sales strategies for each account including Key Accounts and International Accounts;
- Identify sales opportunities by identifying end-user requirements; define market, competitor's share and competitor's strengths and weaknesses; forecast projected business; establish targeted market share;
- Manage new key accounts in all Latin America, North America, Africa and Middle East;
- Sales forecasting, lead generation, heavy prospecting and strategic account management through the close cycle;
- Participation in national and international fairs and events.

- Responsible for the Indirect Sales area.
- Building and maintaining relationships and strategic alliances with channel partners/dealers;
- Identifying and implementing new points of sales;
- Meeting and exceeding established sales goals;
- Creating and executing strategy to improve the sales and CX;
- Managing a team of Channel Sales Managers to insure that goals are achieved;

- Responsible for the Outbound Sales area (direct channel, indirect channel and partnerships);
- Building and maintaining relationships and strategic alliances with channel partners/dealers;
- Lead and contribute to strategic commercial negotiation (core listing, annual pricing, payment terms, cost savings, supply agreements);
- Driving deep into BR segments to identify and manage strategic business opportunities;
- Understand specific market and customer environment and specific customer activities, strategies, brands, markets, consumers via multisource (public information, annual reports, press, meetings, etc.);
- Development of new opportunities (cross and up selling) within the customer portfolio;
- Managing a team of channel sales managers and inside sales managers to insure that goals are achieved;
- General management responsibilities.

- Develop KAM strategies aligned with organizational objectives;
- Analyze markets and identify opportunities to expand business with strategic accounts;
- Conduct and support negotiations for long-term commercial contracts, ensuring mutual benefits;
- Monitor the performance of key accounts and implement measures to optimize results;
- Collaborate with other departments such as sales, CS, marketing, and operations to ensure an integrated approach;
- Build and maintain strategic relationships with stakeholders and c-levels in key accounts, ensuring customer satisfaction and loyalty.
- Engage in participation at conferences, fairs and events to enhance brand visibility and networking opportunities.

- Scoping new markets in the region; advising and executing on entry and implementation strategy;
- Developing strategic partnerships with regulators, key operational and growth partners in all LatAm region;
- Collaborate closely with the founders to meet objectives around product experience, growth, and scalability through LatAm region;
- Drive day-to-day execution to successfully launch and grow in new markets, being hands-on with end-to-end care delivery, including recruitment of employees, qualifying assignments, and upholding perfect fulfilment rates and care quality;
- Research and develop a deep understanding of the differentiated value proposition of Onfly´s services in the context of potential markets, including addressable size, readiness and competitiveness landscape;
- Independently articulate and champion the state of play of the markets we expand into. Define market-level OKRs and seek support and alignment from leadership and operational teams;
- Executing scale operations and working with cross-functional teams in our BR office; from Operations to Finance, Legal and Compliance, Marketing and Communications, etc.
- Identify business expansion opportunities in Key Accounts through up sell and/or cross sell (Brazil <> LatAm);
- Build and maintain strategic relationships with stakeholders and c-levels in Onfly´s Key Accounts, ensuring customer satisfaction and loyalty.
- Engage in participation at conferences, international fairs and events to enhance brand visibility and networking opportunities.

- Develop and execute the strategic business plan for Mexico, focusing on market expansion, client acquisition and revenue growth;
- Build and maintain strategic relationships with key stakeholders, including regulatory bodies, financial institutions, and industry partners;
- Negotiate and execute commercial partnerships, ensuring mutually beneficial agreements;
- Coordinate with lawyers, accountants, and tax experts to ensure compliance and operational efficiency;
- Lead and manage all aspects of operations, including sales, customer support, marketing campaigns, and partnership development;
- Analyze performance results and implement continuous improvements to optimize processes;
- Drive brand awareness and engagement through targeted marketing initiatives, social media channels, and community events;
- Monitor market trends, competitor activities, and regulatory developments to identify opportunities and mitigate risks;
- Provide leadership, mentorship, and support to the local team, fostering a culture of excellence, innovation, and collaboration;
- Stay updated on local regulations and licensing requirements, assessing their impact on the business;
- Participate in industry events and professional organizations to expand networks and represent the company.

- Developed the backend infrastructure including: the client-server system, the parallel computing system, and the distributed file systems to support the Orbeus online API platform and several mobile applications; Developed and a large-scale database system for data management;
- Researched on a variety of computer vision and machine learning problems, including face recognition, scene and object understanding, etc.

Orbeus helps computers see like human beings. Orbeus developed one of the most advanced computer visual recognition engine that enables computers to perform face detection/recognition, logo and products recognition, optical character recognition and scene understanding. Orbeus was selected to participate Excelerate Lab Incubator in Chicago in Summer 2012. It is now acquired by Amazon. More info: www.rekognition.com.

Managed loan portfolios and monitored customer repayment schedules; 
Conducted financial assessments and field verification for loan applicants; 
Maintained accurate client records and prepared operational reports; 
Built and maintained strong relationships with customers.

